meta {
  name: requisition status report
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}reports/requisition-status/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~export: csv
  ~status: ORDERED
  ~project: 1
  ~date_from: 2026-09-01
  ~date_to: 2026-09-30
  ~p: 1
  ~page_size: 25
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Requisitions grouped by status with ageing (FR-9.2): each row has
  `days_in_current_status` and `age_days` (since created). `summary` gives the
  count and average days in status for every status. Admin or Manager.
  Filters: `status`, `project`, `date_from` / `date_to` (created date).

  Like every report (FR-9.1): a paginated JSON table with `columns` (key and header)
  and, where it applies, a `summary`. Add `?export=xlsx` or `?export=csv` to download
  the whole report (every page) as a file; quantities are written with their unit symbol.

  ## API example response
  {
